# Visual Output Verification

For tasks that generate or modify visual output (plots, figures, UI screens, rendered images):
- Run the code to produce a concrete visual artifact (screenshot or image file).
- Use OCR/Computer Vision inspection on that artifact before marking the task complete.
- If text labels are required (axes, annotations, symbols), confirm they are visible and readable.
- If visuals are missing or unclear, iterate until the output is verifiably present.
- Check contrast (yellow on white is bad, dark blue on black etc)